  "label": "Hypersexualization",
  "description": "The meme relies on the hypersexualization of the Black father figure, portraying him as sexually explicit and crude in his response to a child's innocent question. This stereotype reduces a father's role to one of sexual gratification and objectifies his body and behavior, which is offensive and degrading. It aligns with the broader anti-Black stereotype of hypersexualization, which falsely associates Black men with excessive or inappropriate sexual behavior.",
